Year = {2019},
Volume = {3},
Number = {1},
Pages = {9-12},
Abstract = {The Robert Wood Johnson Foundations' Culture of Health represents a
   national call to ensure everyone living in the United States can have a
   healthy life. This article discusses how organizations outside of the
   health care sector can participate in creating a Culture of Health by
   using a nonprofit organization (Little Village Environmental Justice
   Organization) as an example. The organization's role in policy creation
   concerning cross-sector partnerships and governance to create equitable
   communities was of primary importance to this article. The example
   presented has important public health implications, particularly as it
   relates to promoting healthy outcomes among urban Latinx community
   members.},
